# Hello Needle native components

This build of Hello Needle @PROJECT_VERSION@ targets @CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME@ on @CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR@. It links to the platform's Qt @qt_version@ Core, Gui and Widgets libraries. Qt and the native Qt platform plugin are installed separately. Poppler supplies the separate `pdftotext` and `pdftoppm` commands. Antiword supplies the `antiword` command and its character maps.

The application and worker are distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later. The original Clapgrep attribution appears in `NOTICE.md`. The Rust code linked into the worker is inventoried in `LICENSES/rust/DEPENDENCIES.md`. Individual notices and license texts are available offline under `LICENSES/`. Each CI binary has a companion source archive containing the exact project revision, the build scripts and its vendored Rust dependencies. Platform-managed packages provide the separate libraries, plugins and converters with their own licenses, source packages and update procedures.

`BUILD-ENVIRONMENT.json` in a native package identifies its Git revision, operating system, linked libraries, converter versions, and the installed versions of the following packages. Qt's translation package supplies standard Spanish widget and dialog text.

| Component | Upstream source |
| --- | --- |
| Qt libraries, native plugins and translations | [Qt Base](https://code.qt.io/cgit/qt/qtbase.git/) · [Qt Translations](https://code.qt.io/cgit/qt/qttranslations.git/) |
| Poppler command-line utilities | [Poppler source](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/poppler/poppler) |
| Antiword and its character maps | [Antiword source and distribution revisions](https://sources.debian.org/src/antiword/) |

The package revision identifies the distribution's own patches and build files. These catalogs make those materials available.

| Distribution | Sources and build recipes |
| --- | --- |
| Ubuntu 24.04 | [Qt Base](https://packages.ubuntu.com/source/noble/qt6-base) · [Qt translations](https://packages.ubuntu.com/source/noble/qt6-translations) · [Poppler](https://packages.ubuntu.com/source/noble/poppler) · [Antiword](https://packages.ubuntu.com/source/noble/antiword) |
| FreeBSD | [Qt Base](https://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/tree/devel/qt6-base) · [Qt translations](https://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/tree/devel/qt6-translations) · [Poppler utilities](https://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/tree/graphics/poppler-utils) · [Antiword](https://cgit.freebsd.org/ports/tree/textproc/antiword) |
| MSYS2 UCRT64 | [Qt Base](https://packages.msys2.org/base/mingw-w64-qt6-base) · [Qt translations](https://packages.msys2.org/base/mingw-w64-qt6-translations) · [Poppler](https://packages.msys2.org/base/mingw-w64-poppler) · [Antiword](https://packages.msys2.org/base/mingw-w64-antiword) |
| Homebrew | [Qt Base](https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/qtbase) · [Qt translations](https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/qttranslations) · [Poppler](https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/poppler) · [Antiword](https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/antiword) |
| MacPorts | [Qt Base](https://ports.macports.org/port/qt6-qtbase/) · [Qt translations](https://ports.macports.org/port/qt6-qttranslations/) · [Poppler](https://ports.macports.org/port/poppler/) · [Antiword](https://ports.macports.org/port/antiword/) |
